# Expected Utility Illustrated: A Graphical Analysis of Gambles with More than Two Possible Outcomes

**Authors:** Chen, Frederick H.

## Abstract
The author presents a simple geometric method to graphically illustrate the expected utility from a gamble with more than two possible outcomes. This geometric result gives economics students a simple visual aid for studying expected utility theory and enables them to analyze a richer set of decision problems under uncertainty compared to what they typically see in an intermediate-level microeconomics course. (Contains 7 figures.)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ872060

